[…], London: […] Humphrey Robinson, […], and for Humphrey Moseley […], published 1647, →OCLC, (please specify the act number in uppercase Roman numerals, and the scene number in lowercase Roman numerals):"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ʍaɪl/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/waɪl/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/wæl/", "tags": ["US", "conjunction", "unstressed"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/wɑl/", "tags": ["US", "conjunction", "unstressed"]}], "forms": [{"word": "whiles", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "whiling", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "whiled", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "whiled", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "(transitive, now only in combination with away; see also while away) To pass (time) idly.", "tags": ["in compounds", "transitive"], "examples": ["I whiled away the hours whilst waiting for him to arrive"], "quotes": [{"text": "Some were whiling the time by admiring the figures on the cloth of tissue.", "reference": "1839, Robert Folkestone Williams, The Youth of Shakespeare, page 184:"}, {"text": "Here in seclusion, as a widow may, / The lovely lady whiled the hours away, […]", "reference": "1863 November 23, Henry Wadsworth Longfellow, “The Student’s Tale. The Falcon of Ser Federigo.”, in Tales of a Wayside Inn, Boston, Mass.: Ticknor and Fields, →OCLC, page 35:"}, {"text": "As if she was just whiling her time with them until his arrival.", "reference": "2018, Shukla Lal, Floating Logs:"}], "synonyms": ["idle", "laze", "lounge"], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(transitive) To occupy or entertain (someone) in order to let time pass.", "tags": ["transitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "They whiled them with such answere as suted to their purposes, and long adoe was made in weaving and unweaving Penelopes web, till the Spanish Armada was upon the Coast, and the very Ordnance proclaimed in their eares a surcease from further illusions.", "reference": "1588, Samuel Purchas, Hakluytus Posthumus or, Purchas his Pilgrimes:"}, {"text": "He sat her on the corner of the carpenter's bench, and parried or diverted her questions about her father, and the desirability of wakening him by handing her the long curled shavings; and when these palled, he whiled her on by the impossible task of teaching him her version of the 'Three Golden Balls' a blank-verse poem, but rhythmically intoned, which he had taught her.", "reference": "1907, Barbara Baynton, edited by Sally Krimmer and Alan Lawson, Human Toll (Portable Australian Authors: Barbara Baynton), St Lucia: University of Queensland Press, published 1980, page 130:"}, {"text": "In other worlds I whiled me now Through many a dark night long.", "reference": "2010, Dr Rudolf Steiner, Truth-Wrought-Words:"}, {"text": "Like a good father, he whiled him with stories about the past of his nation and discussed in detail the intricacies of his profession, teaching the child secrets of the craft that had been passed from generation to generation.", "reference": "2018, Michael Joyce, Yada:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(intransitive, archaic) To elapse, to pass.", "tags": ["archaic", "intransitive"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "The tedious hours whiled slowly on, 'till the succeeding afternoon, when the expected carriage made its appearance much sooner than they had promised themselves.", "reference": "1764, Mrs. Gunning (Susannah), Family Pictures, a Novel. Containing Curious and Interesting Memoirs of Several Persons of Fashion in W-----re, page 115:"}, {"text": "Years whiled. He aged, sank, sickened; and was not: / And it was said, 'A man intractable / And curst is gone.'", "reference": "1901, Thomas Hardy, “A Man”, in Poems of the Past and the Present:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "verb", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ʍaɪl/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/waɪl/", "tags": []}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/wæl/", "tags": ["US", "conjunction", "unstressed"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/wɑl/", "tags": ["US", "conjunction", "unstressed"]}], "forms": [{"word": "whiles", "tags": ["present", "singular", "third-person"]}, {"word": "whiling", "tags": ["participle", "present"]}, {"word": "whiled", "tags": ["participle", "past"]}, {"word": "whiled", "tags": ["past"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "Alternative spelling or misspelling of wile.", "tags": ["alt of", "alternative", "misspelling"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "There it lies before me sparkling in the sun, whiling me as it often does from my pen or book to gaze upon its loveliness.", "reference": "1842, “Letters from Italy: No. 1 —Nice”, in The Dublin University Magazine, volume 19, page 47:"}, {"text": "Perhaps the coziness of his seat, and the absence of the sun's rays from the side of the house where he was seated, had some agency in whiling him into a delicious sleep;", "reference": "1860, The Knickerbacker - Volume 56, page 593:"}, {"text": "Upon the shelf before me stands, The Book that lured to distant Lands, That prompt my boyish wish to roam, And whiled me from my childhood's home.", "reference": "1880, Ann Bagwill Cuming, Night Thoughts and Day Dreams, page 10:"}, {"text": "“Do not let us go near them,\" he says in a cajoling, low voice to Bertha, whiling her away into the sun and the flowers;", "reference": "1900, Christian Work: Illustrated Family Newspaper - Volume 68, page 38:"}, {"text": "He whiled him on to speak farther; but the same cloud was still upon Sir Henry Dacre's mind.", "reference": "2020, George Payne Rainsford James, Agincourt: A Romance:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/while", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}